From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 22:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/pm: Update SMU14_0_2 driver if version to 0x33 for R9700

The SMU firmware on retail Radeon AI PRO R9700 (gfx1201, 0x1002:0x7551)
ships with interface version 0x33 (51), but the mainline driver hardcodes
0x2E (46). This results in BACO entry failures, fan control silently
ignored (109°C reached without fan response), and idle power stuck at
+220W per node.

Reported in:
  - https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/issues/5908
  - https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/issues/6101
  - https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/issues/6078

Tested on: Radeon AI PRO R9700, Talos Linux v1.12.7 (kernel 6.18.24)

This is a minimal 1-line change. The message ID mapping was already
extended for v51 compatibility by commit 37a45fb8db26 ("drm/amd/pm:
update message interface for smu v14.0.2/3"). SmuMetrics_t struct
verification is recommended but mismatch is non-fatal in this scenario
(metrics may show stale values).

Signed-off-by: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/inc/smu_v14_0.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/inc/smu_v14_0.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/inc/smu_v14_0.h
index aaaaaaaaaaaa..bbbbbbbbbbbb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/inc/smu_v14_0.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/inc/smu_v14_0.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 #define SMU14_DRIVER_IF_VERSION_INV 0xFFFFFFFF
 #define SMU14_DRIVER_IF_VERSION_SMU_V14_0_0 0x7
 #define SMU14_DRIVER_IF_VERSION_SMU_V14_0_1 0x6
-#define SMU14_DRIVER_IF_VERSION_SMU_V14_0_2 0x2E
+#define SMU14_DRIVER_IF_VERSION_SMU_V14_0_2 0x33

 #define FEATURE_MASK(feature) (1ULL << feature)

--
2.45.0
